WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:24.000
I feel that there have been a large number of fairly well-qualified, or exceptionally well-qualified

00:25.000 --> 00:33.000
people who have seen objects that have not had any really logical explanation other than

00:33.000 --> 00:34.000
this.

00:34.000 --> 00:41.000
I think that maybe in fact each and every one of them does have an explanation, but I think

00:41.000 --> 00:47.000
that there are so many possibilities, so many thousands of possibilities of other planets

00:47.000 --> 00:53.000
out somewhere in the universe that would have a livable atmosphere that I would hate

00:53.000 --> 00:55.000
to rule out.

00:55.000 --> 01:02.000
The possibility that maybe there are people or some type of human life on some of these.

01:02.000 --> 01:07.000
And if this is the case, then it's not too unfeasible to think that perhaps some of

01:07.000 --> 01:11.000
these objects might have been something of this time.

01:11.000 --> 01:17.000
You don't think that the comparatively short step out into space that the Mercury flight

01:17.000 --> 01:23.000
will take you on is far enough out to make any observations in this area.

01:23.000 --> 01:32.000
No, I think we're still at a fairly low order of getting out into space when you regard

01:32.000 --> 01:38.000
when you speak of space and being millions of miles involved, and we're only getting out a hundred

01:38.000 --> 01:39.000
miles or so.

01:39.000 --> 01:42.000
What about the so-called plan effect?

01:42.000 --> 01:51.000
The snowflakes, the fireflies, both the Sharon Carpenter seem to feel that it's frost

01:51.000 --> 02:00.000
or some nature off of the capsule, but apparently Glenn still sort of cast doubt on that theory.

